n><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t3-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>other types of food supplement.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t3-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>different genetic strains of mice.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t3-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>varying amounts of exercise.</span></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":5},{"id":"en-c19-t3-l-g3-1","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 26-30","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>Complete the flowchart below.</p><p><i>Choose&nbsp;<b>FIVE</b>&nbsp;answers from the box and write the correct letter,&nbsp;<b>A-H</b>.</i></p><div><table><colgroup><col></colgroup><tbody><tr><td><p>Choose mice which are all the same <span class=\"source-question-item\"><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">26</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t3-l-q26\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></span>.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>⭣</p><div><table><colgroup><col></colgroup><tbody><tr><td><p>Divide the mice into two groups, each with a different <span class=\"source-question-item\"><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">27</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t3-l-q27\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></span>.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>⭣</p><div><table><colgroup><col></colgroup><tbody><tr><td><p>Put each group in a separate cage.</p><p>Feed group A commercial mouse food.</p><p>Feed group B the same, but also sugar contained in <span class=\"source-question-item\"><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">28</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t3-l-q28\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></span>.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>⭣</p><div><table><colgroup><col></colgroup><tbody><tr><td><p>Take measurements using an electronic scale.</p><p>Place them in a weighing chamber to prevent <span class=\"source-question-item\"><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">29</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t3-l-q29\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></span>.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>⭣</p><div><table><colgroup><col></colgroup><tbody><tr><td><p>Do all necessary <span class=\"source-question-item\"><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">30</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t3-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></span>.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"options-dnd-panel dnd-panel dnd-panel--inline\"><div class=\"dnd-panel-instruction\">Drag and drop an option to fill in each blank.</div><div class=\"dnd-cards-container\"><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"A\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">A.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">size</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"B\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">B.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">escape</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"C\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">C.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">age</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"D\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">D.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">water</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"E\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">E.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">cereal</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"F\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">F.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">calculations</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"G\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">G.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">changes</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"H\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">H.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">colour</span></div></div></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"></div>","sourceQuestionCount":5}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/cambridge-ielts-19-academic-listening-3-audio-3.mp3"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-c19-t3-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/161247-cambridge-ielts-19-academic-listening-3-audio-4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-c19-t3-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"diagram_labelling","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p><i>Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer.</i></p><p><strong>Microplastics</strong></p><p><strong>Where microplastics come from</strong></p><p>fibres from some <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t3-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> during washing</p><p>the breakdown of large pieces of plastic</p><p>waste from industry</p><p>the action of vehicle tyres on roads</p><p><strong>Effects of microplastics</strong></p><p>They cause injuries to the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t3-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> of wildlife and affect their digestive systems.</p><p>They enter the food chain, e.g., in bottled and tap water, <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t3-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> and seafood.</p><p>They may not affect human health, but they are already banned in skin cleaning products and <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t3-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> in some countries.</p><p>Microplastics enter the soil through the air, rain and <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t3-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</p><p><strong>Microplastics in the soil – a study by Anglia Ruskin University</strong></p><p>Earthworms are important because they add <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t3-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> to the soil.</p><p>The study aimed to find whether microplastics in earthworms affect the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t3-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> of plants.</p><p>The study found that microplastics caused:</p><p><span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t3-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> loss in earthworms</p><p>fewer seeds to germinate</p><p>a rise in the level of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t3-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> in the soil.</p><p>The study concluded:</p><p>soil should be seen as an important natural process.</p><p>changes to soil damage both ecosystems and <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t3-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/cambridge-ielts-19-academic-listening-3-audio-4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-c19-t3-l-q1","part_id":"en-c19-t3-l-p1","group_id":"en-c19-t3-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"harbour/harbor","correct_answer_variants":["harbour","harbor"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_154859_1","order_index":1,"points":1},{"id":"en-c19-t3-l-q2","part_id":"en-c19-t3-l-p1","group_id":"en-c19-t3-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"bridge","correct_answer_variants":["bridge"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[2],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_154859_2","order_index":2,"points":1},{"id":"en-c19-t3-l-q3","part_id":"en-c19-t3-l-p1","group_id":"en-c19-t3-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"3.30/3:30/three thirty/half 3/three","correct_answer_variants":["3.30","3:30","three thirty","half 3","three"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[3],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_154859_3","order_index":3,"points":1},{"id":"en-c19-t3-l-q4","part_id":"en-c19-t3-l-p1","group_id":"en-c19-t3-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"Rose/rose","correct_answer_variants":["Rose","rose"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[4],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_154859_4","order_index":4,"points":1},{"id":"en-c19-t3-l-q5","part_id":"en-c19-t